## [1.12.0] - 2026-08-02

- Fixed sender override: the plugin now captures the sender resolved by the `wp_mail_from` / `wp_mail_from_name` filters (e.g. configured in WooCommerce email settings) at queue time and stores it as a "From" header. Previously the profile's "From" address/name always won because the filters run after the `pre_wp_mail` interception.
- A "From" header is only injected when the sender email was actually overridden, so generic emails without a custom sender still fall back to the profile's configured "From" address.

## [1.11.1] - 2026-07-08

- Improved first-tick scheduling: `getDefaultLastTick` now dynamically calculates the default elapsed time based on the configured rate, ensuring at least 2 email slots on the first tick regardless of rate or unit setting.

## [1.11.0] - 2026-05-10

- Added configurable email log row limit (max rows stored in the database).
- Added option to automatically clear subject, message, and headers of sent emails to save database space.
- Added database migration to clean content of already-sent emails on existing installations.

## [1.10.3] - 2026-04-29

- Fixed filter action handling so "Bypass Scheduling" sends matching emails immediately.
- Fixed "Set Scheduler Priority" filter action to schedule queued emails after applying the priority override.
- Improved immediate-send return values so SMTP failures are reported instead of always returning success.
- Improved recipient parsing for arrays and comma/semicolon-separated recipient strings.
- Hardened address parsing to avoid undefined values for malformed addresses.

## [1.10.2] - 2026-04-11

- Added AJAX polling for the system status bar on the settings page (refreshes every 30 seconds).
- Added spinner animation while loading status data.
- Fixed language file locale notation (sk_SK instead of fr_FR).

## [1.10.1] - 2026-04-02

- Wordpress admin notices displayed next to the main headline on the settings page bugfix.

## [1.10.0] - 2026-04-02

- Added "Filtered" status for emails that match filter rules set to "Do Not Send" action.
- Email logs now display the "filtered" status with distinct styling.
- Status donut chart includes "filtered" count.
- Database migration automatically adds the new status to existing installations.

## [1.9.0] - 2026-03-31

- Added "Enable email scheduler" option in General Settings. When disabled, emails are sent immediately instead of being queued (default: enabled).
- Added new "Filters" tab for email filtering rules.
- Filters allow matching emails by subject, body, or recipient using plain text or regex patterns.
- Filter actions: Bypass Scheduling (send immediately), Do Not Send (discard), Set Priority (custom queue priority).
- Filter rules can be prioritized, enabled/disabled individually.
- Added Slovak translations for new features.

## [1.8.1] - 2024-11-13

- Added an authentication mode selector for SMTP profiles with support for password-less (trusted relay) connections.
- Skipped username/password validation when authentication is set to none.
- Mailer now disables SMTP authentication and clears credentials for password-less profiles.

## [1.8.0] - 2024-11-12
- Initial public release with SMTP profile management, queuing, retries, and logging.
